{"type":"text","timestamp":1788463202341,"sessionID":"ses_f974d9641ffeYfNBhdx33Io0s3","part":{"id":"prt_068b6afc4001tBhq5UGlDl5Okv","messageID":"msg_068b6a402001P36SJY37zhEIiR","sessionID":"ses_f974d9641ffeYfNBhdx33Io0s3","type":"text","text":"Done. The `StopIteration` crash is fixed:\n\n**Root cause:** `CellCollection.__init__` at `mesa/experimental/cell_space/cell_collection.py:52` unconditionally called `next(iter(self._cells.keys()))`, which raises `StopIteration` when the collection has no cells (e.g., after `.select(filter_func)` matches nothing).\n\n**Changes:**\n- `_capacity` is now `int | None` — set to `None` when the collection is empty, otherwise taken from the first cell (unchanged behavior for non-empty collections).\n- Added a public read-only `capacity` property exposing `int | None` so empty collections report capacity as unavailable.\n- Added `test_empty_cell_collection` in `tests/test_cell_space.py` covering direct initialization with `[]`, empty results from `.select()`, and confirming non-empty collections keep their capacity.\n\n**Verification:** All 231 tests pass (224 + 7 matplotlib components), and formatting is clean — the 5 ruff warnings are pre-existing on the base commit.","time":{"start":1788463198148,"end":1788463202334}}}
